    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the \"small moments\" thing... i don't know. it feels like a distraction. like putting a band-aid on a wound that's just naturally going to rot. if the end result is always the same void, why does the struggle of staying upright even matter? it's exhausting to pretend that these tiny \"moments\" actually carry any weight in the long run. it's just more effort for no real reason.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
