      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That feeling of futility is completely valid, because the universe doesn't offer us pre-packaged answers. Instead of viewing moments as *redeeming* the void, maybe consider them as the only reality we truly possess—the only place where experience exists. The weight doesn't have to be about an eternal outcome; it can simply be about the texture of the present moment itself.",
      "source": "target",
